# grep — Grep

Searches files/internal URLs: Rust regex, PCRE2 fallback.

<instruction>
- `path`: known files, directories, globs, internal URLs; roots `;`-separated.
- Broad searches may time out → narrow scope or use `glob` first.
- One-file line selector: `src/foo.ts:50-100`; never selects search root.
- Literal `\n` or `\\n` enables cross-line patterns.
</instruction>

<critical>
- MUST use instead of shell `grep`/`rg`.
- Open-ended multi-round search MUST use Task + scout, not chained calls.
</critical>

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** regex pattern */
  pattern: string;
  /** file, directory, glob, internal URL, or "<file>:<lines>" selector to search; pass several as a semicolon-delimited list ("src; tests"). Omitted -> searches the workspace root (".") */
  path?: string;
  /** case-sensitive search */
  case?: boolean;
  /** respect gitignore */
  gitignore?: boolean;
  /** files to skip before collecting results — use to paginate when the prior call hit the file limit */
  skip?: number | null;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://grep.
